1
00:04:54,545 --> 00:05:00,545
And now the film…

2
00:09:49,090 --> 00:09:55,090
Jesus Christ Superstar is a drama, history film directed by Norman Jewison.

3
00:14:43,636 --> 00:14:49,636
As played out by a theatre troupe, the last days of Jesus Christ are
depicted from the perspective of Judas Iscariot, his betrayer.

4
00:19:38,181 --> 00:19:44,181
As Jesus' following increases, Judas begins to worry that Jesus is falling for his own hype, forgetting
the principles of his teachings and growing too close to the prostitute Mary Magdalene.

5
00:24:32,727 --> 00:24:38,727
Jesus Christ, played by Ted Neeley.

6
00:29:27,272 --> 00:29:33,272
Judas Iscariot, played by Carl Anderson.

7
00:34:21,818 --> 00:34:27,818
Mary Magdalene, played by Yvonne Elliman.

8
00:39:16,363 --> 00:39:22,363
Pontius Pilate, played by Barry Dennen.

9
00:44:10,909 --> 00:44:16,909
Caiaphas, played by Bob Bingham.

10
00:49:05,454 --> 00:49:11,454
Simon Zealotes, played by Larry Marshall.

11
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Jesus Christ Superstar is a 1973 American musical Biblical drama film directed by Norman
Jewison, co-written by Jewison and Melvyn Bragg, and choreographed by Robert Iscove.

12
00:58:54,545 --> 00:59:00,545
It is based on the 1970 concept album written by Tim Rice and composed by
Andrew Lloyd Webber, which in turn spawned the 1971 stage musical.

13
01:03:49,090 --> 01:03:55,090
The film depicts the conflict between Judas and Jesus and the emotions and motivations
of the main characters during the week of the crucifixion of Jesus.

14
01:08:43,636 --> 01:08:49,636
It stars Ted Neeley, Carl Anderson, Yvonne Elliman and
Barry Dennen in the principal roles.

15
01:13:38,181 --> 01:13:44,181
Jesus Christ Superstar premiered at the Uptown Theater in Washington D.C.

16
01:18:32,727 --> 01:18:38,727
on June 26, 1973, and was released theatrically in
the United States on August 15, 1973.

17
01:23:27,272 --> 01:23:33,272
Despite criticism from a few religious groups and mixed reviews
from critics, the film was a box office success.

18
01:28:21,818 --> 01:28:27,818
Neeley, Anderson, and Elliman were nominated for Golden Globe Awards in 1974, for
their portrayals of Jesus, Judas, and Mary Magdalene, respectively.

19
01:33:16,363 --> 01:33:22,363
The film was also nominated for Best Motion Picture – Musical or
Comedy, and received an Oscar nomination for Best Score.

20
01:38:10,909 --> 01:38:16,909
The film explores themes of dance, israel, christianity, crucifixion, musical.

21
01:43:05,454 --> 01:43:11,454
The tone is emotional.
